## Running FantasyBumps
Install the requirements with: `pip install -r requirements.txt`.

Next, run the `ppy init [--dev-team]` command.
This command migrates the database and installs fixed data (such as seat values).
With the `--dev-team` flag, a user/team can also be loaded for development.

    Username: DevTeam
    Password: password

Games are created with:

    ppy game_start --eights | --torpids | --demo [--date YYYY-MM-DD | --year YYYY]

where the first flag (e.g. `--torpids`, `--eights`) indicates which series the event belongs to.
`--demo` is also available as a series option which will use fixed data for demonstration/testing purposes.
However, it requires an empty database and further options are ignored.
By default, the created event will start in five days time, but this can be overridden with the `--date` flag.
Alternatively, to create an event using data from an event in a previous year, use the `--year` flag.
These latter two options cannot be used simultaneously.


#### Development
Install the pre-requisites with: `pip install -r requirements.txt`

This project defines useful commands via `project.py`, (which also provides a gateway to Django's `manage.py`). Hereafter, these commands are written as `ppy xyz`.

A development game can be initiated & advanced 24 hours with:
`ppy devgame:start`
`ppy devgame:advance`

If required, a user/team can be created with: `ppy loaddata dev_team`
